# Architecture documentation rules

When editing `Docs/**`:

1. Navigate from `Docs/.brain/INDEX.md`; update CONCEPTS / LINKS / GLOSSARY for
   new durable ideas.
2. Keep depth in `knowledge/` and `tech-space/`; keep `.brain` short.
3. New architecture-style pages: when-to-use, monorepo mapping, Mermaid/C4
   diagram, trade-offs, link to related styles and rules.
4. New design-pattern pages: intent, structure diagram, toy example, this-repo
   placement, anti-patterns.
5. ADRs live in `Docs/tech-space/decisions/` — context, decision, consequences.
6. Implementation steps belong in `walkthrough/` or `clouds/` with commands + why.
7. Do not contradict `architecture-rules.md` or open ADRs without calling it out.
